leafy green thorn tips. Exact colours: main amber (#a08a6a), secondary dark orange (#4a3a2a), accent lime (#a0d070). ROW 2 = \"Vine Snapper\" (territorial guardian of its patch): A carnivorous plant: a bulbous green pod on a short stem with a huge Venus-flytrap mouth, no eyes, and six whipping vine tentacles around the base. Green leaves with dark green veins, pink-red inner mouth with thorny teeth. Exact colours: main green (#3a8a3a), secondary dark green (#1a3a1a), accent red (#ff5a8a). ROW 3 = \"Dusk Wolfling\" (small swarm creature that attacks in packs): A small lean wolf cub with a long body, four legs, a bushy tail and pointed ears, snarling with tiny fangs. Two glowing yellow eyes. Slate-blue-grey fur, dark navy back, yellow eye glow. Its ears are big for its head, its paws are oversized, and its tail is fluffy. A snarling puppy. Exact colours: main blue (#4a4a6a), secondary dark blue (#1a1a2a), accent amber (#ffd040). ROW 4 = \"Wisp Sprite\" (ranged spitter/caster that keeps its distance): A floating ghost-light sprite: a teardrop-shaped jelly body with two big glowing eyes, three ribbon-like tail tentacles. Mint-teal body, dark teal core, white glowing aura and sparkles. Its body is see-through with a bright heart of light inside, its eyes are big and friendly, and tiny sparkles trail behind it. Exact colours: main teal (#5affd0), secondary dark teal (#1a6a5a), accent white (#ffffff). REMEMBER: in every row the legs visibly move through columns 1-6 (stride, push-off, foot up passing, opposite stride, push-off, foot up passing), and columns 7-9 bite (open wide, lunge, snap shut). Style: retro 16-bit video game sprite (SNES / Game Boy Advance era), a real game asset rather than an illustration: chunky visible square pixels on a low-resolution grid, no anti-aliasing, no blur, no gradients, no painterly or soft shading, flat colour areas with at most 3 shades per colour, limited palette of about 16-24 colours, clean 1-pixel dark outline, hue-shifted shading (shadows lean violet-blue, highlights lean warm), strong readable silhouette, cute-but-dangerous fantasy monster. Background: isolated on a perfectly flat solid magenta #FF00FF background (no gradient, no floor, no cast shadow). No text, labels, numbers, frame borders, motion lines or effects.",
     "followup": "The legs barely move in columns 1-6. Redraw the SAME sprite sheet: the same 4 characters with exactly the same designs, colours, sizes, order and layout (4 rows x 9 columns, magenta background), and keep columns 7-9 as they are. Change ONLY the legs in columns 1-6, seen from the side so every foot is visible: column 1 = STRIDE A: near front leg reaching far forward and near back leg stretched far back, all feet on the ground, a clear gap of background under the belly (this cell is also the character's main sprite, so make it the cleanest pose); column 2 = PUSH-OFF A: body dips lowest, the near back foot lifting off the ground behind; column 3 = PASSING A: the near back leg swings forward under the belly with its foot high in the air and knee bent, body at its highest; column 4 = STRIDE B: the opposite pair now leads, far front leg reaching forward and far back leg stretched back, near legs under the body (clearly different from column 1); column 5 = PUSH-OFF B: body dips lowest, the far back foot lifting off the ground behind; column 6 = PASSING B: the far back leg swings forward under the belly with its foot high in the air, body at its highest. Two-legged characters: columns 1 and 4 a long stride with opposite legs in front, columns 2 and 5 the back foot lifting, columns 3 and 6 one knee raised high as the legs pass. Characters without legs: column 1 squashed flat and wide, column 2 leaning forward, column 3 stretched tall and thin, column 4 squashed flat again, column 5 leaning forward, column 6 stretched tall. Tails, wings and tentacles swing with every step. Make each leg pose big, obvious and different from the others; a lifted foot must be clearly in the air with background visible under it.",
