     "prompt": "Pixel art SPRITE SHEET of WALK and BITE animations for a 2D game. Layout: a wide grid of exactly 5 rows and 9 columns of equal square cells filling the whole image; leave a clear empty gap of background between every cell; do not draw grid lines. Each ROW is one character, always the same design, colours and size; only its pose changes from column to column. Every character faces RIGHT, full body, side view (profile, seen from the side, at most slightly from above) so every leg and foot is fully visible below the body, feet on the bottom of its cell, the same ground line in all 9 cells. ANIMATION, the same for every row. Columns 1-6 are a looping WALK CYCLE. The LEGS MUST BE IN A CLEARLY DIFFERENT POSITION IN EACH OF COLUMNS 1-6: this is the most important rule, look-alike poses are wrong. Exaggerate the leg poses like a classic cartoon walk so the difference reads even at a tiny size. column 1 = STRIDE A: near front leg reaching far forward and near back leg stretched far back, all feet on the ground, a clear gap of background under the belly (this cell is also the character's main sprite, so make it the cleanest pose); column 2 = PUSH-OFF A: body dips lowest, the near back foot lifting off the ground behind; column 3 = PASSING A: the near back leg swings forward under the belly with its foot high in the air and knee bent, body at its highest; column 4 = STRIDE B: the opposite pair now leads, far front leg reaching forward and far back leg stretched back, near legs under the body (clearly different from column 1); column 5 = PUSH-OFF B: body dips lowest, the far back foot lifting off the ground behind; column 6 = PASSING B: the far back leg swings forward under the belly with its foot high in the air, body at its highest. Two-legged characters: columns 1 and 4 a long stride with opposite legs in front, columns 2 and 5 the back foot lifting, columns 3 and 6 one knee raised high as the legs pass. Characters without legs: column 1 squashed flat and wide, column 2 leaning forward, column 3 stretched tall and thin, column 4 squashed flat again, column 5 leaning forward, column 6 stretched tall. Tails, wings and tentacles swing with every step. Columns 7-9 are a BITE ATTACK: column 7 = WIND-UP, head and body pulled back and crouched, jaws or mouth opened as wide as possible showing every tooth; column 8 = LUNGE, body stretched forward to the right, jaws still wide open around the target; column 9 = SNAP, head fully forward, jaws clamped shut, body leaning into the bite. Each row is a DIFFERENT species; all 5 live in the Sunken Ruins (A city of a forgotten race, now home to eels), so they share that setting's mood and palette family, but each must have its own clearly different body shape and silhouette. THE CHARACTERS, follow every detail: ROW 1 = \"Ruin Eel\" (hungry predator that hunts): A long sea eel with six segments, two side fins, two glowing eyes and a toothy jaw, with ancient carved stone patterns on its skin. Dark teal body, near-black shadows, yellow glowing markings. Exact colours: main dark teal (#2a5a5a), secondary near-black (#0e2a2a), accent amber (#ffe05a). ROW 2 = \"Drowned Knight\" (territorial guardian of its patch): A drowned undead knight: an upright figure in barnacle-crusted armour with two legs, two arms, a horned helmet with two horns and a seaweed plume crest, two glowing eyes in the visor. Teal-grey armour, dark teal shadows, mint-green glow. Exact colours: main teal (#4a6a6a), secondary dark teal (#1a2a2a), accent light teal (#7affd0). ROW 3 = \"Jelly Drifter\" (harmless grazing prey): A drifting jellyfish with a large translucent bell, no eyes and six long frilly tentacles. Pink-violet body, dark purple inner organs, glowing pale pink edges. Its bell is see-through with glowing pink veins, and the frilly tentacles trail long and wavy beneath it. It drifts calmly, bobbing in place. Exact colours: main light purple (#e07aff), secondary purple (#6a2a7a), accent white (#ffd0ff). ROW 4 = \"Siren Fry\" (skittish prey that runs away): A small fish with an egg-shaped body, two fins, a fanned tail and two big eyes. Sky-blue scales, dark blue back, pale yellow belly and fin edges. Its fins are long and flowing like ribbons, the scales sparkle, and a small glowing yellow lure hangs from its forehead. Exact colours: main cyan (#5ab0e0), secondary dark cyan (#1a4a6a), accent light amber (#fff0a0). ROW 5 = \"Coral Horde\" (small swarm creature that attacks in packs): A small round coral creature with four little legs, two eyes and five branching coral spikes on its back. Coral-pink body, dark red shadows, cream tips. Its little body is knobbly like real coral with tiny polyps, its legs are short crab-like stubs, and it looks small but feisty. Drawn as one creature. Exact colours: main light red (#ff7a6a), secondary red (#7a2a2a), accent white (#ffe0d0). REMEMBER: in every row the legs visibly move through columns 1-6 (stride, push-off, foot up passing, opposite stride, push-off, foot up passing), and columns 7-9 bite (open wide, lunge, snap shut). Style: retro 16-bit video game sprite (SNES / Game Boy Advance era), a real game asset rather than an illustration: chunky visible square pixels on a low-resolution grid, no anti-aliasing, no blur, no gradients, no painterly or soft shading, flat colour areas with at most 3 shades per colour, limited palette of about 16-24 colours, clean 1-pixel dark outline, hue-shifted shading (shadows lean violet-blue, highlights lean warm), strong readable silhouette, cute-but-dangerous fantasy monster. Background: isolated on a perfectly flat solid magenta #FF00FF background (no gradient, no floor, no cast shadow). No text, labels, numbers, frame borders, motion lines or effects.",
     "followup": "The legs barely move in columns 1-6. Redraw the SAME sprite sheet: the same 5 characters with exactly the same designs, colours, sizes, order and layout (5 rows x 9 columns, magenta background), and keep columns 7-9 as they are. Change ONLY the legs in columns 1-6, seen from the side so every foot is visible: column 1 = STRIDE A: near front leg reaching far forward and near back leg stretched far back, all feet on the ground, a clear gap of background under the belly (this cell is also the character's main sprite, so make it the cleanest pose); column 2 = PUSH-OFF A: body dips lowest, the near back foot lifting off the ground behind; column 3 = PASSING A: the near back leg swings forward under the belly with its foot high in the air and knee bent, body at its highest; column 4 = STRIDE B: the opposite pair now leads, far front leg reaching forward and far back leg stretched back, near legs under the body (clearly different from column 1); column 5 = PUSH-OFF B: body dips lowest, the far back foot lifting off the ground behind; column 6 = PASSING B: the far back leg swings forward under the belly with its foot high in the air, body at its highest. Two-legged characters: columns 1 and 4 a long stride with opposite legs in front, columns 2 and 5 the back foot lifting, columns 3 and 6 one knee raised high as the legs pass. Characters without legs: column 1 squashed flat and wide, column 2 leaning forward, column 3 stretched tall and thin, column 4 squashed flat again, column 5 leaning forward, column 6 stretched tall. Tails, wings and tentacles swing with every step. Make each leg pose big, obvious and different from the others; a lifted foot must be clearly in the air with background visible under it.",
