     "prompt": "Single game character sprite, 96x96 pixels, three-quarter top-down view, full body, idle pose, facing right, centred with a few pixels of padding. Subject: \"Plaguewing\", the player's evolution form at stage 5 of 10 â€” Its wingbeats scatter poisoned dust. Appearance: A plague moth-beetle with a fat armoured body, six legs and four large ragged insect wings shedding purple poison dust. Four eyes, curled proboscis-like jaws, a short stinger tail. Dark green body, olive wing veins, purple glowing spots on the wings. The wings are moth-like with eye-spot patterns, frayed at the edges, and a cloud of purple sparkling dust trails behind. Furry collar around the neck, segmented abdomen with glowing bands. Exact colours: main green (#3e8a26), secondary dark green (#1e3614), accent indigo (#a03aff). Theme: toxic horror: dripping venom, warty slick skin, sickly glowing sacs and stingers. It should look clearly more evolved and medium-sized than earlier forms of its line. Style: retro 16-bit video game sprite (SNES / Game Boy Advance era), a real game asset rather than an illustration: chunky visible square pixels on a low-resolution grid, no anti-aliasing, no blur, no gradients, no painterly or soft shading, flat colour areas with at most 3 shades per colour, limited palette of about 16-24 colours, clean 1-pixel dark outline, hue-shifted shading (shadows lean violet-blue, highlights lean warm), strong readable silhouette, cute-but-dangerous fantasy monster. isolated on a perfectly flat solid magenta #FF00FF background (no gradient, no floor, no cast shadow).",
