     "prompt": "Single game character sprite, 96x96 pixels, three-quarter top-down view, full body, idle pose, facing right, centred with a few pixels of padding. Subject: \"Astral Beholder\", the player's evolution form at stage 7 of 10 â€” A floating eye that unmakes what it stares at. Appearance: An astral beholder: a large floating sphere dominated by one huge central eye, with eight eye-stalks/tentacles each tipped with a small eye, two horns and a toothy grin. Violet-indigo body, dark navy shadows, glowing pink irises. Its central eye has a glowing pink iris and a slit pupil, the eye stalks curl like snakes, and its horns are crescent-shaped. A wide grin of pointed teeth sits below the central eye. Exact colours: main indigo (#4a2ab0), secondary dark indigo (#180c48), accent light purple (#ff7aff). Theme: spellborn beast: glowing runes, floating sparks of magic, ethereal translucent fins and eyes; pure astral line: cosmic eyes, starlight, gravity-bending aura. It should look clearly more evolved and medium-sized than earlier forms of its line. Style: retro 16-bit video game sprite (SNES / Game Boy Advance era), a real game asset rather than an illustration: chunky visible square pixels on a low-resolution grid, no anti-aliasing, no blur, no gradients, no painterly or soft shading, flat colour areas with at most 3 shades per colour, limited palette of about 16-24 colours, clean 1-pixel dark outline, hue-shifted shading (shadows lean violet-blue, highlights lean warm), strong readable silhouette, cute-but-dangerous fantasy monster. isolated on a perfectly flat solid magenta #FF00FF background (no gradient, no floor, no cast shadow).",
