     "sheet": "Horizontal sprite sheet of 6 walk-cycle frames of the same character, each frame 96x96 pixels, side view (profile, seen from the side, at most slightly from above) so every leg and foot is fully visible below the body, full body, walking, facing right, identical design in every frame, centred with a few pixels of padding. Subject: \"Wraithmaw\", the player's evolution form at stage 7 of 10 â€” Inhales souls along with the air. Appearance: A wraithmaw: a ghostly upper body with two clawed arms and no legs, trailing four smoky tentacles, two horns. A huge mouth sucking in green soul wisps, two glowing eyes. Dark purple robes of smoke, near-black shadows, green soul-fire. Its jaw unhinges like a snake's, its arms are long and thin with claw fingers, and its horns curl like a ram's. Green souls swirl into its mouth. Exact colours: main dark purple (#4a2458), secondary near-black (#1a0c20), accent green (#5aff7a). Theme: spellborn beast: glowing runes, floating sparks of magic, ethereal translucent fins and eyes; lich line (arcane fused with venom): skeletal, ghostly green soul-fire, cursed bloom. It should look clearly more evolved and medium-sized than earlier forms of its line. Style: retro 16-bit video game sprite (SNES / Game Boy Advance era), a real game asset rather than an illustration: chunky visible square pixels on a low-resolution grid, no anti-aliasing, no blur, no gradients, no painterly or soft shading, flat colour areas with at most 3 shades per colour, limited palette of about 16-24 colours, clean 1-pixel dark outline, hue-shifted shading (shadows lean violet-blue, highlights lean warm), strong readable silhouette, cute-but-dangerous fantasy monster. isolated on a perfectly flat solid magenta #FF00FF background (no gradient, no floor, no cast shadow). The LEGS MUST BE IN A CLEARLY DIFFERENT POSITION IN EACH OF FRAMES 1-6: this is the most important rule, look-alike poses are wrong. Exaggerate the leg poses like a classic cartoon walk so the difference reads even at a tiny size. frame 1 = STRIDE A: near front leg reaching far forward and near back leg stretched far back, all feet on the ground, a clear gap of background under the belly (this cell is also the character's main sprite, so make it the cleanest pose); frame 2 = PUSH-OFF A: body dips lowest, the near back foot lifting off the ground behind; frame 3 = PASSING A: the near back leg swings forward under the belly with its foot high in the air and knee bent, body at its highest; frame 4 = STRIDE B: the opposite pair now leads, far front leg reaching forward and far back leg stretched back, near legs under the body (clearly different from frame 1); frame 5 = PUSH-OFF B: body dips lowest, the far back foot lifting off the ground behind; frame 6 = PASSING B: the far back leg swings forward under the belly with its foot high in the air, body at its highest. Two-legged characters: frames 1 and 4 a long stride with opposite legs in front, frames 2 and 5 the back foot lifting, frames 3 and 6 one knee raised high as the legs pass. Characters without legs: frame 1 squashed flat and wide, frame 2 leaning forward, frame 3 stretched tall and thin, frame 4 squashed flat again, frame 5 leaning forward, frame 6 stretched tall. Tails, wings and tentacles swing with every step.",
