     "prompt": "Single game character sprite, 64x64 pixels, three-quarter top-down view, full body, idle pose, facing right, centred with a few pixels of padding. Subject: \"Mire Crab\", a territorial guardian of its patch living in the Glowcap Marsh. Appearance: A muddy swamp crab with a wide flat shell, six walking legs and two big uneven pincers raised defensively, two eyes on stalks. Mud-brown shell with darker cracks and moss, orange-tipped claws. Its shell is covered in mud and reeds, one claw is much bigger than the other, and bubbles rise from its mouth. Exact colours: main orange (#7a5a3a), secondary dark orange (#3a2a1a), accent orange (#ff9a5a). Fits the Glowcap Marsh setting (Spores drift like snow over the sucking mud). Style: retro 16-bit video game sprite (SNES / Game Boy Advance era), a real game asset rather than an illustration: chunky visible square pixels on a low-resolution grid, no anti-aliasing, no blur, no gradients, no painterly or soft shading, flat colour areas with at most 3 shades per colour, limited palette of about 16-24 colours, clean 1-pixel dark outline, hue-shifted shading (shadows lean violet-blue, highlights lean warm), strong readable silhouette, cute-but-dangerous fantasy monster. isolated on a perfectly flat solid magenta #FF00FF background (no gradient, no floor, no cast shadow).",
